---

Feature harnesses get a model session only from `createFeaturePiSession` (`src/agent/runtime/createFeatureSession.ts`), which resolves model policy, a durable `eventSink`, `attachReportObstacle`, and abort via `attachSessionAbort` over `createPiSession` (`piSession.ts`). It does not wrap `send` with checkpoint or snapshot persistence; `checkpointId` is a send/event field only. Only `src/agent/runtime/` may import `piSessionImpl.ts`, `runAgentLoop`, or build a pi-ai stream (ADR 0023). `ToolPolicy.allowBuiltin` is the literal type `false` in `types.ts`: no shell, write, edit, or filesystem built-in reaches a session. Register the full tool set at create time; phase gating happens in executors through `src/review/orchestrator/phaseToolPolicy.ts`, never by swapping active tools mid-session (ADR 0025). `src/effect/server.ts` must not reach `piSession.ts` or `modelsJson.ts` (`test/architectureRules.test.ts`). `send` rejects on a settled unrecovered provider error.
